# Never put a website CTA tab in the footer

## Hard rule

**Never** put a big “Visit the HTSA website” / `footer-site-cta` button or tab in the footer of any page CJ sends to a prospect.

That includes:
- Precall pages (`r/<slug>/`, `before-our-call/`, templates)
- Close / enrollment pages
- Due diligence / resource pages

CJ has said this repeatedly. It looks terrible. Do not revive it from old clones.

## What to do instead

If the HTSA website needs to be reachable:

1. Prefer it inside **All HTSA Resources** / proof area (subtle, not hero-level)
2. Or as a **small text link** in the same footer row as YouTube / Instagram / Facebook (same size, no big green button)

## Templates that must stay clean

When cloning or editing:

- `r/_TEMPLATE-precall.html`
- `before-our-call/index.html`
- `templates/_TEMPLATE-close.html`
- `access/index.html`

Strip any `footer-site-cta` / “Visit the HTSA website” block before shipping.

## Pre-ship check

Grep the new file for `footer-site-cta` and `Visit the HTSA website`. Zero matches.
